    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d155">

                <pb facs="0407" n="311" xml:id="pg311"/>

                <head>No. 153.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Fish to Mr. Williams.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1874-10-23"><hi rendition="#italic">October</hi> 23,
                        1874</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 191.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to your dispatch No. 54, in
                    relation to the case of Walter Jackson, who was charged with the crime of piracy
                    and assault with intent to commit murder on board a British vessel on the high
                    seas, I inclose for your information a copy of an instruction<anchor n="*"
                        xml:id="d155-f1"/> of this date, addressed by the Department to Mr. George
                    F. Seward, the consul-general of the United States at Shanghai, in reference to
                    this case.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>HAMILTON FISH.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d155-f1" n="*" xml:id="d155-f1-content">
                <p>See instruction No. 424 to consul-general at Shanghai.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
